  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a direct relationship between the compound in question and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, mediated through the CD70 antigen. This compound is identified as a target of multiple molecular entities, including a complex of (2S)-1-O-3,6,9,12,15-Octadecapentaenoyl-2-O-6,9,12,15-Octadecatetraenoyl-3-O-Beta-D-Galactopyranosylsn-Glycerol and triacontan-15-ol. These molecules are all known to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, indicating a potential mechanism of action where the compound may act as a ligand or modulator of this epigenetic complex. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, highlighting a shared pathway of targeting CD70 antigen, which in turn interacts with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that the compound may function as a modulator of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, potentially influencing epigenetic regulation through interactions with CD70 antigen.",
